{
  "_readme": [
    "Ground truth for ROI-cropped captures taken through the app itself.",
    "",
    "This is the input the backend actually receives. The other ground-truth",
    "file scores full-frame photographs, which are a harder and unrepresentative",
    "case: the app crops to the ROI window before uploading.",
    "",
    "Conventions match real_labels.json: a value means the pack prints it, null",
    "means the pack genuinely has no such field, and an omitted key means the",
    "capture is not legible enough to assert a truth and is therefore not",
    "scored.",
    "",
    "Note the 'unlabelled' entries. Roughly a third of these packs print bare",
    "inkjet stamps with no field names at all - two dates, a price and a code,",
    "in a fixed order and nothing to match an alias against. MRP, manufacturing",
    "date and expiry date are present on every one of them, so those three have",
    "to be recoverable by position and shape rather than by label."
  ],
